# Macroeconometrics and Time Series Analysis Project

This project was developed as part of a Master’s degree coursework in Applied Economics at the University of Lille.

The objective of this project is to apply macroeconometric and time series methods to the analysis of macroeconomic indicators and stochastic processes.

The project includes both empirical and theoretical econometric exercises using real economic data and autoregressive process modeling.

## Main Topics
- Macroeconomic time series analysis
- FEDFUNDS interest rate analysis
- Economic growth and unemployment dynamics
- Stationarity analysis
- AR(1) and AR(2) processes
- Yule-Walker equations
- ACF and PACF interpretation
- Simulation of stochastic processes

## Methods Used
- Time series visualization
- Autocorrelation analysis
- Partial autocorrelation analysis
- Stochastic process simulation
- Econometric interpretation

## Tools Used
- R
- Quantmod
- GGplot2
- Econometric and statistical methods

## Files Included
- R code
- Final report (PDF)
- Graphical analysis

This project reflects practical skills in macroeconometrics, stochastic process analysis, time series modeling and quantitative economic analysis.
